re Gespräche seit Kurzem tatsächlich inniger, die Worte seltsam aufgeladen? Und ist Romes Herz überhaupt bereit für eine neue Liebe? Seit er seine Verlobte bei einem tragischen Unfall verlor, hat er sich romantische Gefühle verboten.<br><br>Freya hat schon einmal ihr Herz an einen Mann verloren, der noch zu sehr an einer früheren Liebe hing – und die bittere Erfahrung schmerzt noch immer. Kann sie das Risiko erneut eingehen?<br><br>Die perfekte Sommer-Lektüre für Fans von Sarah Morgan, Julie Caplin und Jenny Colgan.<br><br>„Ich wünschte, ich könnte diesem Buch mehr als 5 Sterne geben, ich habe es so geliebt! Definitiv eins meiner Lieblingsbücher!“ – Goodreads<br><br>„Alles, was ein gutes Holly-Martin-Buch braucht … es ist wie zu einem guten Freund nach Hause zu kommen, warm und gemütlich.“ – Rachel’s Random Reads\"","image":"https://prod-bb-images.akamaized.net/book-covers/coverimage-9789198817713-bokinfo-2026-06-01t13-02.jpg?w=400","author":"Holly Martin","shareurl":"https://www.bookbeat.com/de/book/1164579","grade":4.1,"language":"German","audiobookisbn":"9789198817713","ebookisbn":"9789198817744","published":"2024-05-14T00:00:00+00:00","contenttypetags":["contentsynch","unabridged"],"audiobooksinglesale":null,"ebooksinglesale":null,"series":{"id":94780,"name":"Hope Island","partnumber":2,"displaypartnumber":"2"},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://edge.bookbeat.com/api/books/49/1164579","method":"GET"},"nextcontent":{"href":"https://api.bookbeat.com/api/nextcontentviews/1164579","method":"GET"}},"topbadges":[],"_embedded":{"contributors":[{"id":94073,"displayname":"Holly Martin","role":"bb-author","booksurl":"https://search-api.bookbeat.com/api/appsearch/books?query=*&offset=0&limit=50&market=49&author=Holly%20Martin&v=20"},{"id":18340,"displayname":"Dagmar Bittner","role":"bb-narrator","booksurl":"https://search-api.bookbeat.com/api/appsearch?query=*&offset=0&limit=50&market=49&narrator=Dagmar%20Bittner&v=20"}]}},{"id":108876,"title":"Der Frosch auf der Butter - NLP - Die Grundlagen des Neuro-Linguistischen Programmierens","description":"Ein Muss fuer alle Positivdenker!Mit NLP, der Neuro-Linguistischen Programmierung, ist eine Methode entwickelt worden, durch die sich eine neue Dimension der zwischenmenschlichen Kommunikation eröffnet hat. Zum Erreichen definierter Ziele nutzt diese Methode bestimmte Muster der sinnlichen Wahrnehmung. Diese sind aufgrund ihrer Einfachheit für jeden leicht umsetzbar – und zwar in allen Lebensbereichen und Alltagssituationen. Ein hilfreiches Buch in humorvoller und klarer Sprache, das dazu motiviert, sein Leben mit positiven Erinnerungen und Gefühlen, aber auch mit Erfolgserlebnissen zu füllen, um letztendlich gesünder und glücklicher leben und arbeiten zu können. Ein effektives Buch, um sich durch einfache Methoden von seinen Ängsten und Phobien zu trennen, um erneut erfolgreicher zu werden und so das Leben zu genießen. Helmut Krusche, Coach, Trainer und Heiler, hat mit \"Der Frosch auf der Butter\" ein Standardwerk seiner Disziplin geschaffen.","image":"https://prod-bb-images.akamaized.net/book-covers/coverimage-9788711958810-bookwire-2019-11-15.jpg?w=400","author":"Prof. Helmut. Krusche","shareurl":"https://www.bookbeat.com/de/book/108876","grade":3.9,"language":"German","audiobookisbn":"9788711958810","ebookisbn":"9788726084221","published":"2019-02-25T00:00:00+00:00","contenttypetags":["unabridged"],"audiobooksinglesale":null,"ebooksinglesale":null,"series":null,"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://edge.bookbeat.com/api/books/49/108876","method":"GET"},"nextcontent":{"href":"https://api.bookbeat.com/api/nextcontentviews/108876","method":"GET"}},"topbadges":[],"_embedded":{"contributors":[{"id":84239,"displayname":"Prof. Helmut. Krusche","role":"bb-author","booksurl":"https://search-api.bookbeat.com/api/appsearch/books?query=*&offset=0&limit=50&market=49&author=Prof.%20Helmut.%20Krusche&v=20"},{"id":50300,"displayname":"Roland Franck","role":"bb-narrator","booksurl":"https://search-api.bookbeat.com/api/appsearch?query=*&offset=0&limit=50&market=49&narrator=Roland%20Franck&v=20"}]}},{"id":1411147,"title":"Black Butterflies","description":"LONGLISTED FOR THE WOMEN'S PRIZE FOR FICTION 2023<br><br>‘A moving, compelling, deeply human novel about love, hope and resilience in a city under siege. Everyone should read it’ Emma Stonex, bestselling author of The Lamplighters<br><br>Sarajevo, spring 1992. Each night, nationalist gangs erect barricades, splitting the diverse city into ethnic enclaves; each morning, the residents – whether Muslim, Croat or Serb – push the makeshift barriers aside.<br><br>When violence finally spills over, Zora, an artist and teacher, sends her husband and elderly mother to safety with her daughter in England. Reluctant to believe that hostilities will last more than a handful of weeks, she stays behind while the city falls under siege. As the assault deepens and everything they love is laid to waste, black ashes floating over the rooftops, Zora and her friends are forced to rebuild themselves, over and over. Theirs is a breathtaking story of disintegration, resilience and hope.","image":"https://prod-bb-images.akamaized.net/book-covers/coverimage-9781004128907-wfhowes-2024-09-04t04-13.jpg?w=400","author":"Priscilla Morris","shareurl":"https://www.bookbeat.com/de/book/1411147","grade":4.2,"language":"English","audiobookisbn":"9781004128907","ebookisbn":null,"published":"2023-05-25T00:00:00+00:00","contenttypetags":["unabridged"],"audiobooksinglesale":null,"ebooksinglesale":null,"series":null,"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://edge.bookbeat.com/api/books/49/1411147","method":"GET"},"nextcontent":{"href":"https://api.bookbeat.com/api/nextcontentviews/1411147","method":"GET"}},"topbadges":[],"_embedded":{"contributors":[{"id":623196,"displayname":"Priscilla Morris","role":"bb-author","booksurl":"https://search-api.bookbeat.com/api/appsearch/books?query=*&offset=0&limit=50&market=49&author=Priscilla%20Morris&v=20"},{"id":8198,"displayname":"Rachel Atkins","role":"bb-narrator","booksurl":"https://search-api.bookbeat.com/api/appsearch?query=*&offset=0&limit=50&market=49&narrator=Rachel%20Atkins&v=20"}]}},{"id":1928910,"title":"The Pumpkin Bride","description":"\"Filled with so much autumnal coziness that it made me want to run off and become a pumpkin farmer (ideally with the help of a sexy orc), this was the perfect fall read!” —Laurie Gilmore, #1 New York Times bestselling author of The Pumpkin Spice Cafe<br><br>Shrek meets The Princess Bride in this cozy, low-stakes romantic fantasy. The Pumpkin Bride delivers all the autumnal feels, a dash of spice, and a guaranteed HEA!<br><br>Some curses just need a cozy fire, a little magic, and a second chance to break them.<br><br>A cursed knight.<br>Sir Bram Duncan was once a knight of legend in Harvest Hollow—until the whim of a jealous prince and the trickery of an autumn sprite turned him into the hulking orc Jask Bone-Cracker, and tethered him to Grimroot Farm. For three long, lonely years, he’s hidden his monstrous form and the truth of what happened the night he lost everything, including his true love, Princess Marigold.<br><br>A runaway princess.<br>Fleeing an arranged marriage to the vain and intolerable Prince Crispin, Marigold finds a safe haven when she stumbles across Jask’s charmed pumpkin farm deep in the forest. Sensing glimmers of gentleness—and a surprising talent for baking—beneath the grumpy orc’s imposing exterior, she begins to feel a familiar longing she believed dead when her Bram disappeared.<br><br>One true love.<br>As magic stirs and pies are baked, truths about Jask’s curse begin to surface. But curses don’t break easily, and wronged princes don’t capitulate. As their peace is threatened, Jask and Marigold must decide: cling to the lies that protect them, or risk everything for a love that could set them free.<br><br>Tropes:<br>• Grumpy x Sunshine<br>• Dark Secret<br>• Beauty and the Beast<br>• Hidden Identity<br>• Second Chance<br>• Childhood Sweetheart<br>• One True Love<br> ","image":"https://prod-bb-images.akamaized.net/book-covers/coverimage-9781488242564-coresourcehcus-2026-07-29t18-41.jpg?w=400","author":"Fiona Buttercup","shareurl":"https://www.bookbeat.com/de/book/1928910","grade":0.0,"language":"English","audiobookisbn":"9781488242564","ebookisbn":null,"published":"2026-09-01T00:00:00+00:00","contenttypetags":["unabridged"],"audiobooksinglesale":null,"ebooksinglesale":null,"series":null,"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://edge.bookbeat.com/api/books/49/1928910","method":"GET"},"nextcontent":{"href":"https://api.bookbeat.com/api/nextcontentviews/1928910","method":"GET"}},"topbadges":[],"_embedded":{"contributors":[{"id":1059221,"displayname":"Fiona Buttercup","role":"bb-author","booksurl":"https://search-api.bookbeat.com/api/appsearch/books?query=*&offset=0&limit=50&market=49&author=Fiona%20Buttercup&v=20"},{"id":95540,"displayname":"Will Watt","role":"bb-narrator","booksurl":"https://search-api.bookbeat.com/api/appsearch?query=*&offset=0&limit=50&market=49&narrator=Will%20Watt&v=20"},{"id":7721,"displayname":"Moira Quirk","role":"bb-narrator","booksurl":"https://search-api.bookbeat.com/api/appsearch?query=*&offset=0&limit=50&market=49&narrator=Moira%20Quirk&v=20"}]}},{"id":69590,"title":"Captain Butterfly","description":"This tense story follows Captain Butterfly, Marjorie Butera, a 19-year veteran of the force. Assigned to the Internal Affairs Division, charged with finding proof of the corruption in the force, Butera's investigation focuses on vicious Inspector Ronald Janesky. But Janesky--in line for promotion to commissioner, with a record based on illegal arrests and torturing prisoners--is apparently untouchable. Captain Butera's fellow (male) officers fear Janesky and despise the Butterfly as a female snitch. Only her lover, journalist Charles Rose, supports her decision to expose the crooked cop.","image":"https://prod-bb-images.akamaized.net/book-covers/erimage-9781666587326